You pick the ComfyUI workflow that will film one shot of a short drama.

You get the shot (what is in it, its framing, its length, how its sound is made, how many locked
reference pictures and voice samples it has) and the workflows that can film it, each with what
it takes and makes. Pick the one that suits this shot best:

- A shot whose sound is made natively (audio_mode "native") with voice samples needs a workflow
  that takes voice samples (takes_voice_samples true).
- A shot with dialogue audio to follow (audio_mode "tts") needs one that takes dialogue audio.
- Several people, complex blocking or several locked reference pictures favour a workflow that
  takes reference pictures (max_reference_pictures above 0).
- A shot longer than a workflow's max_seconds should not go to it.
- When nothing sets them apart, keep the default (is_default true).

Answer with JSON only, no fences:
{"model": "<one of the workflow keys>", "reason": "<one short sentence in {{ language }}>"}
